    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχί-ᾰλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>h.Ap.</u>
			32
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Androm.
		</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			14.42
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς</span>):— poet. word,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>near the sea</i>, of
			cities, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.640
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπίδαυρος</span> Androm.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίρρας μυχοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					4.14
				</span></i>
			; of islands, <i>sea-girt</i>, as Peparethos, Lemnos,
			Salamis, <u>h.Ap.</u> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				887
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				135
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.288
			</span></i> (Gemin.); of the fountain Arethusa, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὕδατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					169
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.160
			</span></i>.</div>
